    {
      "id": "frag-1",
      "focal_uid": 1,
      "title": "The chokepoint the conflict runs through",
      "insight": "Rising tension points straight at the Strait of Hormuz \u2014 the narrow waterway that carries about a fifth of the world's seaborne oil. From there it flows into both trader nerves and the price itself. It's the physical bottleneck that turns a diplomatic crisis into a real supply scare.",
